--
N5008 [dcl.init.ref]/5.1.1: a function lvalue binds directly to an lvalue
reference to function.  The front end had decayed the function designator
to a pointer before binding and rejected every form (`void (&r)(int) =
cb;' and the global: "bad reference initializer"; the call: a conversion
error).  test_rvalue.desc covers `void (&&)(int)' and a forwarding
reference, test_address.desc that `&cb' does not bind, test_deduced.desc a
deduced `T &' parameter.  bin53: bad reference initializer.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++98), and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
